b.constraint('core_algebra_and_regime_law',['contract_law_api'],'Core graph algebra remains edge, compose, substitute, recurse, fan_out, fan_in, gate, promote, identity and same_object. The seven C constructors and F_D/F_P/F_H selection remain typed inspectable declaration truth with no authority exchange between regimes.',[(0,55,58),(0,69,71)])
b.latitude('host_spelling_variation',['contract_law_api'],['Host spellings may vary only while preserving carrier identity and law.','External tools may realize declared implementation seams.'],['Treating tool metadata, transport configuration or output presence as GTL or ABG authority.'],[(0,55,58),(0,114,116)])
b.constraint('constructive_callable_body',['graph_function'],'Publish the typed outer interface and replayable graph-materializing GTL template; implementation bindings may not replace the constructive body. Recursive functions declare callable relation, termination, foldback, lineage and bounds; HoG traverses that relation and ABG admits child/parent runtime truth, with no hidden recursion controller.',[(0,64,76)])
b.constraint('implementation_seam_denials',['gtl_program'],'Plugin, Worker, handler, tool and native bindings identify only declared seams, I/O contracts, compute means, capability requirements and authority denials. They never own topology, traversal, events, continuation or closure.',[(0,78,82)])
b.constraint('typed_asset_authority',['contract_law_api'],'Prompt construction and other typed assets use GTL contracts with constructor, renderer, digest, authority-slot, output-contract, proof, node and evidence relations. Rendered text is not authority.',[(0,84,87)])
b.constraint('nonlowering_validator',['contract_law_api','gtl_program'],'One deterministic GTL validator applies native-equivalent law to serialized programs and reports typed validity, invalidity or unresolved semantics. Canonical serialization and subordinate indexes are allowed, executable programs and runtime truth are not. It projects declared entry, vector, start-entry, membership, seam, output-admission, consequence and catalog-bind relations without executing them; missing, ambiguous, illegal or incomplete relations remain typed nonconformance.',[(0,89,93),(0,123,127)])
b.constraint('direct_traversal_and_runtime_owner',['gtl_program','graph_function'],'HoG directly traverses original admitted GTL and materialized GraphFunction graphs. Generated HoG programs, CompiledCProgramPlan, compiled execution declarations, ladders and runtime-program catalogs fail as executable authority. ABG owns admission, graph-call/frame identity, effects/result truth, events, replay, evidence, correction, continuation and closure around traversal, without redefining GTL meaning.',[(0,95,103)])
b.constraint('no_downstream_rival_law',['contract_law_api'],'Downstream parsers, prompt prose, adapters, plugins, fixtures and generated read models may not create second contract-law, validator, executor, event, replay, continuation or closure surfaces. Every accepted concrete authored/serialized carrier traces to a GTL declaration, GTL validator rule or ABG runtime-admission contract.',[(0,105,112)])
b.constraint('reload_identity_and_conservation',['contract_law_api'],'PRODUCT.md, GTL README and installed context projections identify this fast reload file with identity sufficient to detect staleness. Validation exposes conservation basis for every traversal bind: intent lineage, target carriers, materialization authority, obligations, residual pressure, dispositions, admission strength and obligation delta. Missing conservation law blocks traversal admission.',[(0,118,133)])
b.constraint('subordinate_declaration_publication',['contract_law_api'],'Requirement, traversal-span, context, destination-topology, test-relation and evidence-policy declarations use existing publication/attachment law. They feed admission/replay but cannot emit events, write ledgers, select traversal or close work.',[(0,135,138)])
b.constraint('capability_owner_matrix',['contract_law_api'],'The declared router assigns topology/starts to GTL Program, callable work to GraphFunction templates/contracts, local transitions to GraphVector, compute interiors to C/regimes, recursion/refinement to GraphFunction relations, effects/results to seams, continuation/closure to GTL policy/result contracts, and domain meaning to downstream Product/Module. GTL validates structure and common law; admission validates effects/results and joins continuation/closure checks. HoG traverses/advances admitted structures, implementations act within interiors, and ABG admits runtime truth, records loci, admits foldback and supplies replay-derived continuation/closure. All downstream work uses the common HoG/ABG path.',[(1,142,151)])
b.constraint('evidence_non_substitution',['contract_law_api'],'Types, lint, reports, package manifests, counts, catalog rows, event co-presence and generated documentation are necessary where applicable, but none substitutes for the installed causal path or complete Product scenarios.',[(2,155,158)])
b.constraint('evaluator_declaration_realization',['evaluator'],'Binding is a declared implementation reference resolved by engine/plugin: GTL owns declaration and engines supply executable realization and provenance. Domain gap, closure, ranking and attestation semantics belong to the declaration and resolved implementation, never the interpreter.',[(5,23,27)])
b.latitude('evaluator_variation',['evaluator'],['Use deterministic, probabilistic or human regimes.','Declare evaluator multiplicity and order at a contract boundary without embedding domain closure meaning in the interpreter.','For a declared sub-scope within one vector, output carriers may include an evaluation scope reference for edge, segment, dimension-cell, fold or relation.'],['Treating scope identity/provenance as event, ledger, traversal-selection or closure authority.'],[(5,21,25),(5,35,35)])
b.constraint('probabilistic_finding_not_closure',['evaluator'],'F_P output under an edge assurance contract is a constrained finding over gain, close disposition, residual pressure, continuation, evidence, authority and composition references. It cannot directly close, write ledgers, select vectors or emit events. Proposed human involvement is a distinct close disposition from ABG F_H-by-absentia for a missing edge assurance contract.',[(5,29,29)],conditions=['Probabilistic evaluator participates in a declared edge assurance contract.'])
b.constraint('evaluator_composition_provenance',['evaluator'],'Composition-participating evaluators preserve regime, role, authority, consumed fields, input/output carrier and evidence references needed by ABG admission. F_P/F_H may emit evidence or judgment under selected composition identity, never deterministic closure authority.',[(5,31,31)],conditions=['Evaluator participates in abg.fn_composition.'])
b.constraint('consumed_field_declarations',['evaluator'],'When deterministic authority placement depends on output fields read by routing, execution construction, pressure projection or closure predicates, expose consumedFieldRefs as an admitted carrier field. An empty set is lawful only if no field-local payload truth is consumed for those decisions.',[(5,33,33)],conditions=['Authority placement depends on consumed output fields.'],exceptions=['Empty consumedFieldRefs is lawful only without such field-local consumption.'])
b.constraint('graph_shape_and_expression',['graph'],'Graph is frozen/immutable with at least id, name, inputs, outputs, nodes, vectors, contexts, rules, effects and tags. Minimal single-step, multistep, refined, composed, recursive and higher-order workflows are all Graph-expressible without a rival single-step ontology. Inputs/outputs are designated boundary nodes; rules/effects carry constraints and declared/derived regime visibility.',[(8,22,28),(8,32,32)])
b.constraint('graph_structural_not_callable',['graph','graph_function'],'Graph is structural substitution/composition unit, not callable work or semantic Job target. Published GraphFunction may materialize it and remains the reusable callable. Public chain is Job -> GraphFunction -> ABG GraphCall -> materialized Graph -> internal GraphVector traversal, never bare Graph execution. Product terms such as overlay/lane/app surface/lifecycle graph must bind back to first-class GTL carriers before claiming GTL/ABG behavior.',[(8,30,38)])
